  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $3.4B in contract spending in FY2027 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs recorded 7,003 awards with an average award size of $489K. Obligations are down 95.9% year over year compared with prior fiscal years. Fiscal history shows obligations of $56.4B in FY22, $61.7B in FY23, $66.9B in FY24, $78.3B in FY25, and $84.3B in FY26. The top spending category for FY2027 to date is Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers at $900M, followed by Wired Telecommunications Carriers at $256M and Other Computer Related Services at $207M. The top vendor by obligations is TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP at $900M, followed by AT&T ENTERPRISES, LLC at $164M and THUNDERCAT TECHNOLOGY, LLC at $142M. Current-year totals are partial because figures are fiscal year to date. This snapshot shows a sharp reduction in obligations in FY2027 to date while category and vendor concentrations remain focused on health, telecommunications, and specialized services.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How large is Veterans Affairs' FY2027 contract spending compared with prior years?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $3.4B in FY2027 to date. Obligations are down 95.9% year over year. Fiscal year obligations were $56.4B in FY22, $61.7B in FY23, $66.9B in FY24, $78.3B in FY25, and $84.3B in FY26. Current-year totals are partial because figures are fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the biggest contract categories and who receives the most obligations?",
        "body": "Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the largest category at $900M, followed by Wired Telecommunications Carriers at $256M and Other Computer Related Services at $207M. TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP is the largest vendor at $900M, followed by AT&T ENTERPRISES, LLC at $164M and THUNDERCAT TECHNOLOGY, LLC at $142M. The Department of Veterans Affairs also obligated funds to logistics, labs, and construction categories represented in the top 10."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Veterans Affairs spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $3.4B in FY2027 to date. The agency recorded 7,003 awards with an average award size of $489K, and obligations are down 95.9% year over year. Prior fiscal years show much larger totals: $56.4B in FY22 through $84.3B in FY26, so current-year figures are partial and reflect fiscal year to date data."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Veterans Affairs buy?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs buys health and medical insurance services, telecommunications, computer services, laboratory instruments and services, couriers, business support services, education services, temporary help, medical laboratories, and building construction. The top categories for FY2027 to date are Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers at $900M, Wired Telecommunications Carriers at $256M, and Other Computer Related Services at $207M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Veterans Affairs's largest contractors?",
      "a": "TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP is the largest contractor at $900M. AT&T ENTERPRISES, LLC is next at $164M and THUNDERCAT TECHNOLOGY, LLC is next at $142M. Other top vendors for FY2027 to date include FEDEX SUPPLY CHAIN DISTRIBUTION SYSTEM, INC. at $102M and LUMEN TECHNOLOGIES GOVERNMENT SOLUTIONS, INC. at $91.3M."
